  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Murlidhar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 14 July, 2022 Author: Anil Verma Bench: Anil Verma 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Anil Verma On The 14th Of July, 2022 Misc. Criminal Case No. 19912 of 2021 Between:- Murlidhar S/O Longar , Aged About 45 Y E A R S , Occupation: Agriculturist Village Datoda, P.S. Simrol (Madhya Pradesh) ..... (By Shri Anendra Singh Parihar, Advocate And The State Of Madhya Pradesh Through Nagar Palika Nigam (Madhya Pradesh) .....Re ( By Shri Shri Sanjay Karanjiwala Ga This application coming on for hearing this day, the court pas following: Order",
    "facts": "Present petitioner has field present petition under section 482 of Cr.P.C of extension of time for compliance of the earlier order dated 16/09/2008 passed in CRR no. 209/2006 passed by this Court. Brief fact of the case is that petitioner/accused has been convicted by the trial Court under section 7(i)(iii) read with section 16(i) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and sentenced to undergo six months rigorous imprisonment with fine of Rs. 1000/-The petitioner preferred an appeal before the Sessions Signature NotCourt, Verified but the same was rejected.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner contended that the petitioner was remained on bail and he was not aware with the order passed by this Court, therefore, he failed to deposit the fine amount as directed by this Court within the stipulated period, therefore, he prays that the order passed by this Court dated 16/09/2008.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner contended that the petitioner was remained on bail and he was not aware with the order passed by this Court, therefore, he failed to deposit the fine amount as directed by this Court within the stipulated period, therefore, he prays that the order passed by this Court dated 16/09/2008.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
